# SPA history-API fallback for static hosts (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).
#
# BrowserRouter serves /app, /explorer and /auth from the client. Those paths do
# not exist as files on disk, so a host that resolves requests against the
# filesystem returns 404 for a direct visit, a page refresh, or a shared deep
# link -- the app only works if the user always arrives at "/" first.
#
# Rewriting every unmatched path to /index.html hands routing back to React
# Router, which then resolves the real path client-side. The Docker image already
# does the equivalent with `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html` in nginx.conf; this
# file covers the static-host deployment path, and vercel.json covers Vercel.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 301/302 (redirect): the browser must keep the original URL
# so React Router sees /explorer rather than /.
/*    /index.html   200
